WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.735
-Hey, guys.
I'm here at a great Irish pub,

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.570
Paddy Reilly's,
here in New York City.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.906
And I'm about to go inside
and meet a great Irish friend

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.641
of mine.
Come on.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.978
[ Irish music plays ]

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.579
Conor?

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:15.281
-Let's go, Seamus!
How are you, man?

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.950
Good to see you, brother!
Good to see you.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.719 line:0%
-Seamus O'Fallon.
-Conor McGregor, as well.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:22.989 line:0%
-Thanks for coming out
and meeting us, buddy.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.691 line:0%
Appreciate it.
-Thank you. It's my pleasure.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.892
This is
Proper No. 12 Irish Whiskey.

00:00:26.892 --> 00:00:29.829
So, the finest manmade
Irish whiskey there is.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.764
-Ah.
-Enjoy, enjoy.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:34.200
-Oh, it's smooth.
Oh, I love this.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.302
-Smooth, yes. So, thank you.
Thank you so much.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.805
-You're getting involved
with this, down to everything.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.273
Why is it called Proper 12?

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.874
-"Proper" is a term we use
in Ireland.

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:44.510
If we say something is
legit, true, it is proper.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:45.811
-It's proper.
-It is proper, exactly.

00:00:45.811 --> 00:00:49.015
And then 12 is the district
I come from, Dublin 12 --

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:50.916
a small little district

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:52.685
full of blue-collar,
hard-working people.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:56.288
It is also home to the largest
children's hospital

00:00:56.288 --> 00:00:57.890
in the country of Ireland.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:01.594
So everyone in Ireland has
a relationship with Dublin 12.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:04.130
And I wanted to pay homage
to where I came from,

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.432
where I learned
the values of hard work,

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:08.701
where I learned loyalty,
where I learned how to fight.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:12.705
And I wanted to pay back and
place the name on my logo --

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.173
Proper No. 12 Irish Whiskey.

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:16.643
-You also give back
to first responders.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:18.478
-Our first responders
are our true heroes.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.513
They are our proper heroes.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:23.115
They are the people
who run into buildings

00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:24.584
as we are running out.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:28.688
So it was only right for me to
give back to these great people.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.990
And, yes, we donate
off of every case sold.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.126
So it's a major operation
to do that, as well.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.527
-That is so cool
that you do that.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:37.563
-It is more and more
that these men and women,

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:39.699
they serve us, they protect us.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.634
They deserve the world and more.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:44.436
-Let's just cut back
to six years ago.

00:01:44.436 --> 00:01:47.841
What was your main income,
six years ago?

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:51.244
-Six years ago, I was
a young Irish kid

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:53.413
working on the building sites
of Ireland.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.682
I was working
as an apprentice plumber.

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.283
So, six years ago.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.485
-You were I plumber
six years ago?

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:00.353
-I was a plumber.
I was a plumber, yes.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.755
-Oh, my God, what a great story.
-Yes, yes.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.124
And actually, funny enough,
only the other day,

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:06.459
for the St. Patrick's Day
parade,

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.726
I was in Chicago,

00:02:07.726 --> 00:02:09.061
and they had me
on the plumbers' float.

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:10.563
-I saw that.
-So I was with the plumbers.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.898
So they gave me a plunger and I
got to represent the plumbers.

00:02:12.898 --> 00:02:15.200
Like, I was
getting the crowd up,

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.569
and then I was pointing back
to the plumbers --

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.472
local plumbers' sign
that was on the float.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.207
-[ Chuckles ]
-So it was absolutely amazing.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.875
I felt like
I had come full circle.

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:25.277
-What gives you the drive
to do this,

00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:27.013
to become the best?

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:30.115
-First of all,
I'm doing what I love.

00:02:30.115 --> 00:02:33.153
I love to compete,
I love to fight, I love clothes,

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:36.088
I love style,
and I love Irish whiskey.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:38.324
My grandfather --
-It's like we're twins!

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.393
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:42.262
I love all the same things
you like.

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:43.896
Yeah, absolutely.
[ Cellphone ringing ]

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:47.667
Oh, sorry, it's my wife calling.
I'm not here.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.602
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.070
You know that old joke, right?

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.705
That will do it,
that will do it.

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.273
-Yes, I love it.

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:56.108
-This is one of my
favorite places to come hang.

00:02:56.108 --> 00:02:58.878
One of the best Guinnesses
in the city, but also --

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:00.846
-Look, I love Guinness,
I love art.

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:02.148
I have big respect to art.

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.949
We used to have a day --
Arthur's Day.

00:03:03.949 --> 00:03:06.986
We should have more days.
We should celebrate more days.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:10.089
For some reason,
Arthur's day was stopped.

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:11.991
And I mean, now that --
since I've been here

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:13.926
for Saint Patrick's week,
here in the U.S.,

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:16.262
in Ireland, we celebrated
Saint Patrick's Day.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.564
But here in the U.S., they
celebrate St. Patrick's week.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:21.801
And it was the best week
of my life.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.603
It was the best week of my life.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:25.304
So, when I get home, I'm gonna
start campaigning.

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:26.839
Let's start adding
more holidays.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.742
Let's start celebrating more.
Celebrate where we come from,

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.578
celebrate our surroundings.
That is the key to success.

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.113
You must celebrate
where you come from.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.716
Be proud of where you come from.
And that's it, so --

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:38.818
-That's right.
-So, today is Proper Day!

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:42.621
[ Laughter ]
The day after Paddy's Day!

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:44.957
-The day after Paddy's Day.
The Proper.

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:46.892
-I'm gonna count the proper
one, two, three, four.

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:49.161
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.
-Right up to 12.

00:03:49.161 --> 00:03:54.600
-It's good to see someone
who just has enormous success

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.602
but also remembers
where they came from,

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:58.337
and you give back.
-Thank you.

00:03:58.337 --> 00:04:00.472
That's what it's about.
You know, nothing --

00:04:00.472 --> 00:04:01.874
I've said this before,
and I said this --

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:04.010
'cause I was
at the Boston game, man,

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.846
I've had such a journey, Seamus.
I'm gonna call you Seamus.

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:09.081
-I love that you call me Seamus.
-I've had such a crazy journey.

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:10.416
I was in the Boston Bruins
locker room.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.118
They sent me in
to help fire them up.

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:14.620
And I was like,
"Nothing heroic gets done.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:15.921
And this is my thought

00:04:15.921 --> 00:04:18.357
on the first-responder situation
that I'm involved in."

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:21.260
I was like, "Nothing heroic.
Heroes are not born

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.829
unless they have a good, solid
support network.

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:25.764
You know, heroes are born
through support,

00:04:25.764 --> 00:04:29.001
through unity,
through guidance and help.

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:30.503
And you know,
the more we support each other,

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.939
the more we unite,
the more we lift each other up,

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:34.873
the more we celebrate
where we come from,

00:04:34.873 --> 00:04:37.677
the more heroic things happen.
The more heroes are born."

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:39.612
-Yeah!
-And that's my thinking of it.

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:42.248
-Oh! By the way, I do love
your style game.

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:43.515
-Thank you. Thanks so much.

00:04:43.515 --> 00:04:44.817
-You always wear
a well-tailored suit.

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:47.519
-Again, it's a passion of mine,
the clothing game.

00:04:47.519 --> 00:04:49.422
I have my own line --
August McGregor.

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:51.490
We're deep in it.
We're on our second drop now.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.993
We're steady building the line.

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:56.328
Again, starting
at the foundations.

00:04:56.328 --> 00:04:59.565
Approach and keep
a beginner's mind, and rise up.

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.067
And that's what
I've done with this,

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.401
that's what I've done
with my clothing.

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:03.769
Obviously, that's what I've
done with the fighting.

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:06.405
You approach every day
in the gym as a beginner.

00:05:06.405 --> 00:05:10.175
You look at people who go to --
Like, the beginners in a gym,

00:05:10.175 --> 00:05:11.877
they always make
the biggest leaps.

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:14.514
Then, they always -- It kind of
filters out a little bit,

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:17.316
The progress slows down.
-Yeah.

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:19.519
-You approach something
with a beginner's mind,

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:21.787
ask questions, think a lot,

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:24.056
learn from
anything and everything,

00:05:24.056 --> 00:05:26.993
like a beginner,
and you grow quicker,

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:28.661
you learn quicker.
And so that's what I'm trying

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:29.929
to do with everything I'm doing.

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.831
-i can't think of a better man

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:34.300
to come to an Irish pub with
than Conor McGregor.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.636
Also, I feel very safe.
I got to be honest.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.004
[ Laughter ]
I feel very, very, very safe.

00:05:39.004 --> 00:05:41.440
-I wore a little flowery shirt.
-Yeah, I know!

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.009
-Tempting them, "Say something!"
-Someone say something!

00:05:44.009 --> 00:05:46.078
-Say something
about my flowery shirt.

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:48.014
-Watch what happens, yeah.
Absolutely.

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:50.649
-That takes true balls.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:53.152
-Let's talk about fighting.
What's next?

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:54.754
We're waiting.
We're waiting for you.

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:56.421
-My next fight,
we're in talks for July.

00:05:56.421 --> 00:05:58.558
We're in talks for July,
so we'll see what happens.

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:01.260
A lot of politics going on.
The fight game is a mad game.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.896
But, again, like I said,
and to my fans,

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:06.231
I am in shape, and I am ready,
so...

00:06:06.231 --> 00:06:08.768
-Do we know who it is yet?
-There are many opponents.

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:11.737
In reality,
I can pick who I please.

00:06:11.737 --> 00:06:13.639
You know, I've done a lot.
I've fought a lot.

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:16.174
I never pulled out of contests.
You know, I've gone through

00:06:16.174 --> 00:06:20.513
some crazy injuries and
crazy external situations

00:06:20.513 --> 00:06:24.317
that many a man would sprint
for the hills

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:26.619
if it happened to them.
But I stood firm

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:28.821
and done my piece
for the company.

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:31.290
So I am in a position now,
there are a lot of --

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.691
Like I said,
this whiskey is my baby.

00:06:32.691 --> 00:06:33.892
I have a lot of great entities.

00:06:33.892 --> 00:06:35.194
I don't necessarily
need to fight.

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:37.029
I am set for life.
My family is set for life.

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:39.465
We are good.
But I am eager to fight.

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:40.833
You know, so we'll
see what happens.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:43.035
I'm just staying ready,
as I like to say.

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:44.904
-You make a lot of people proud,
and we're proud of you.

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:49.175
And as a fellow Irishman,
I thank you very much.

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:51.043
-Thank you, Seamus, my man.
Thank you.

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.477
-Good man.
[ Applause ]

00:06:52.477 --> 00:06:54.146
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

00:06:54.146 --> 00:06:55.815
[ Applause ]

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:58.050
-Hey, should we
go sing a song?

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.486
-Yes, let's sing a song.
What's up, everybody!

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:02.855
-Hey!
-Yo, let's go! Yes!

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:08.093
-♪ I've been a wild rover
for many a year ♪

00:07:08.093 --> 00:07:10.563
♪ And I've spent all my money
on whiskey and beer ♪

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.498
Cheers, everybody!
-Cheers!

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:14.199
I want to go to Dublin
with you once.

00:07:14.199 --> 00:07:17.269
-Yes, please!
I would love that. Let's do it!

00:07:17.269 --> 00:07:19.104
Ireland -- we are
a welcoming nation.

00:07:19.104 --> 00:07:20.305
It would be an honor
to have you over there.

00:07:20.305 --> 00:07:21.740
I would show you around.
-Let's do it!

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:23.308
-Here you go!

00:07:23.308 --> 00:07:25.344
-♪ Nay, never ♪

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:26.645
-1, 2, 3!

00:07:26.645 --> 00:07:29.515
-♪ No, nay, never, no more ♪

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:33.252
♪ Will I play the wild rover ♪

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:37.122
♪ No never, no more ♪

00:07:37.122 --> 00:07:38.891
Conor McGregor, everybody!

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:40.359
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:42.194
Thank you, Paddy Reilly!

00:07:42.194 --> 00:07:45.264 line:0%
Thank you, Proper 12!
Thank you very much!

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:47.066 line:0%
All the best, buddy.

